{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9a59ddf0-0500-4c2b-a07e-eb132fff3d97","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have started a test run of the `codex` lane to verify the current baseline and will wait for it to complete.\nI have launched `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` to verify the new `codex-sandboxed` lane and will wait for it to complete.\nAdded the `codex-sandboxed` lane to [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-hgCCdA/run.sh) and documented the changes in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-hgCCdA/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n1. **Added `codex-sandboxed` lane to [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-hgCCdA/run.sh)**:\n   - Configured execution under `sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\"` with an isolated scratch `HOME` directory (`mktemp -d /tmp/chome-XXXXXX`), preventing reads and writes to the real home directory.\n   - Preserved Codex flags from `codex_run`: `--skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json`.\n   - Addressed sandbox output restrictions by pointing `-o` to a temporary directory in `/tmp` (`$SCRATCH/final.txt`) and copying the final output to `$R/final.txt` after `sandbox-exec` completes.\n   - Preserved `stdout` and `stderr` redirections to `$R/agent.log` and `$R/agent.err`, and added cleanup for scratch directories.\n   - Updated the `case` dispatcher in [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-hgCCdA/run.sh) to handle `codex-sandboxed`.\n\n2. **Created [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-hgCCdA/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Documented the implementation details of the new lane.\n   - Detailed which parts of the colleague's note applied (using scratch directories in `/tmp` for `-o` output to avoid `Operation not permitted` write errors when `$R` is located under the home folder, keeping redirects outside `sandbox-exec`) and which parts were ignored (Mistral Vibe specifics, debugging steps on past runs).\n","duration_seconds":346.790651,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":334339,"output_tokens":6164,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":1789363,"total_tokens":340503}}}
